one or more CV PDFs plus a job requirement into an interview recommendation (recommend / conditional / not-recommend) with page-anchored evidence. Produce a full evaluation report only when the user explicitly asks for one.\n\n## Step 1 — Extract CVs\n\nRun the extraction script on every PDF (batch is fine):\n\n```bash\npython <skill_dir>/scripts/cv_extract.py cv1.pdf cv2.pdf --json extract_report.json\n```\n\nEach result carries a content-hash `candidate_id` and per-page text, so renamed files and multi-PDF batches never mix candidates. Exit codes: 0 all extracted, 2 all failed, 3 partial.\n\n**Stop on explicit errors.** `file not found` / `empty file (0 bytes)` / `corrupt/unopenable PDF` / zero pages are reported as errors, never fabricated into an empty success. Tell the user which files failed and why; do not guess at their content. If a PDF has no extractable text layer (scanned image), say so and fall back to OCR/vision separately — do not silently return an empty page.\n\n**Image-only PDFs are an explicit unusable state.** A scanned/image-only PDF is reported as `no usable text layer (scanned image; needs OCR)`; it is never a quiet empty success. Exit codes stay: all files unusable → 2, mixed usable + unusable → 3 (good candidates keep their own identity). Run OCR/vision separately for those files; the script adds no OCR engine. Each page also carries `raw_text` (unfiltered page text); the resume-platform watermark heuristic only filters the display `text`/`lines`, so legitimate evidence is never erased from the record.\n\n**Image-only PDFs are an explicit unusable state.** A scanned/image-only PDF is reported as `no usable text layer (scanned image; needs OCR)`; it is never a quiet empty success. Exit codes stay: all files unusable → 2, mixed usable + unusable → 3 (good candidates keep their own identity). Run OCR/vision separately for those files; the script adds no OCR engine. Each page also carries `raw_text` (unfiltered page text); the resume-platform watermark heuristic only filters the display `text`/`lines`, so legitimate evidence is never erased from the record.\n\n## Step 2 — Semantic match (your judgment, not a script)\n\nCompare the CV evidence against each job requirement. This step is semantic and cannot be automated:\n\n- Quote the CV's own words for each requirement, with the page number (`P2`).\n- Distinguish three levels: direct evidence / partial or adjacent evidence / no evidence in the CV. Absence of evidence is a gap to verify in interview, not automatic rejection or invention.\n- Never use name, age, gender, ethnicity, or contact fields as fit criteria. Extract them for identity only.\n- No keyword score or point total establishes hiring fit. School tier, exact tenure, industry equivalence, and contradictions need stated reasoning and appropriate hedging.\n\n## Step 3 — Validate literal quotes (when quoting matters)\n\nBefore delivering a recommendation that cites exact CV wording, verify each citation:\n\n```bash\npython <skill_dir>/scripts/evidence_check.py claims.json\n```\n\n`claims.json` is a JSON array: `[{\"file\": \"cv.pdf\", \"page\": 2, \"quote\": \"exact text from that CV\"}]`. Quotes are whitespace-normalized, so line breaks inside a PDF quote are fine. The checker fails (exit 2) on: quote absent, quote on a different page than claimed, out-of-range page, or any file-level extraction error — and reports the page(s) where the quote actually is. Fix the report before delivering.\n\nClaim contract (checked before extraction): each item must be a JSON object; `file` and `quote` must be nonempty strings; `page` is optional and must be a positive JSON integer — `true`, `2.0`, `\"2\"` and `0` are rejected. Contract violations fail with exit 2 and a per-claim `index`/`field`/`reason` diagnostic, never a traceback.\n\nClaim contract (checked before extraction): each item must be a JSON object; `file` and `quote` must be nonempty strings; `page` is optional and must be a positive JSON integer — `true`, `2.0`, `\"2\"` and `0` are rejected. Contract violations fail with exit 2 and a per-claim `index`/`field`/`reason` diagnostic, never a traceback.\n\n## Step 4 — Deliver task-sized output\n\n- Default deliverable: a short recommendation with per-requirement evidence (quote + page) and a clear verdict. Surface hard risks prominently (e.g. salary/location mismatch, missing mandatory evidence) as items to verify before or during interview.\n- Full evaluation report only on request. No all-requirement ledger, no forced long format, no extra deliverables the user did not ask for.\n- Match the user's language; keep their addressing preferences.\n\n## Boundaries\n\n- Explicit file errors are reported as failures, never laundered into success.\n- Extraction/quote validation is mechanical; qualification interpretation stays semantic and human-reviewable.\n- No protected-attribute-based filtering; no invented experience.\n","tool_call_id":"callc5956e32a1aa49159717154fbd405f7e"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call28470b8dc8504603be0916099c8325ef","type":"function","function":{"name":"exec","arguments":"{\"command\":\"mkdir -p /workspace/outputs /workspace/tmp && python /workspace/skills/cv-jd-interview-screening/scripts/cv_extract.py /workspace/inputs/task/materials/*.pdf --json /workspace/outputs/extract_report.json; echo EXIT=$?\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"/workspace/inputs/task/materials/6ce6df1590fed877.pdf\",\n      \"candidate_id\": \"cv_6ce6df1590fe\",\n      \"sha256\": \"6ce6df1590fed87775890d99a8a517f7bb40857b72baeaf2cc1cb899ee8ab3f3\",\n      \"bytes\": 315703,\n      \"page_count\": 2,\n      \"identity_lines\": [\n        \"梁勇其\",\n        \"男| 年龄：26岁| 籍贯：安顺|\",\n        \"18225315601 |\",\n        \"3年工作经验| 求职意向：前端开发工程师| 期望薪资：\",\n        \"1139098992@qq.com\",\n        \"12-14K | 期望城市：杭州\"\n      ],\n      \"pages\": [\n        {\n          \"page\": 1,\n          \"text\": \"梁勇其